{{Yearbox/in-conflicts}}
* In the last battle between [[Shou Lung]] and [[Wa]], the Shou land forces overwhelm those of Wa, but their fleet is grounded on reefs concealed by [[wu jen]] working for the Wa warlords.<ref name=tGHotR-p51>{{Cite book/The Grand History of the Realms|51}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/in-politics}}
* The sixth Emperor Chin of the [[Hai Dynasty]] of [[Shou Lung]] and his court are killed in the fleet's destruction, ending the Hai Dynasty. [[Rourke]], a foreigner piloting the emperor's ship, rescues the [[Emblems of Imperial Authority]] and returns to the [[Imperial City]]. But Rourke is killed  and the Emblems disappear. The [[Black Cycle of Years]] commences in Shou Lung.<ref name=tGHotR-p51 />
*  In [[T'u Lung]], the Black Cycle is characterized by frequent invasions, both from the south and from minor lords in the north, and natural disasters, such as blights, crop failures, and the flooding of the [[Fenghsintzu]]. Order collapses, except where local feudal lords still hold sway. The Wai and Yang clans begin to rise to prominence.<ref name=tGHotR-p51 />


