{{Yearbox/in-conflicts}}
* Above and below ground, vast hordes of [[orc]]s engulf the [[dwarf]] realm of [[Roldilar]], the Realm of Glimmering Swords.<ref name="FRCS2Ep71">{{Cite book/Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting 2nd edition (revised)/A Grand Tour of the Realms|71}}</ref><ref name="tCoRB-p144">{{Cite book/The City of Ravens Bluff|144}}</ref><ref name="FRCS3Ep215">{{Cite book/Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting 3rd edition|215}}</ref> [[Drow]] also strike from the subterranean ways.<ref name="tCoRB-p3">{{Cite book/The City of Ravens Bluff|3}}</ref> [[Deep King]] [[Tuir Stonebeard]] leads the dwarven armies against those of the orcs and [[goblin]]s, but they are defeated at [[Viperstongue Ford]]. Roldilar's defenses are broken, and the dwarves retreat to [[Mount Grimmerfang]].<ref name="FRCS2Ep77">{{Cite book/Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting 2nd edition (revised)/A Grand Tour of the Realms|77}}</ref><ref name="tCoRB-p144"/> This ends in the bloody, 20-day-long [[Battle of Deepfires]] beneath the mountain, and the fall of Roldilar.<ref name="FRCS2Ep77"/><ref name="tCoRB-p144"/><ref name="LEoFp128">{{Cite book/Lost Empires of Faerûn|128}}</ref><ref name="tGHotRp94">{{Cite book/The Grand History of the Realms|94}}</ref>
* [[Human]] and [[elf|elven]] allies save the Roldilarren dwarves from total extinction.<ref name="FRCS2Ep71"/> The elven warrior [[Beluar]] and his forces rout the orcs at Viperstongue Ford, then pursue them through the hills later known as [[Beluar's Hunt]] and into the village of [[Maskyr's Eye]] to slay the last orc.<ref name="FRCS2Ep74">{{Cite book/Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting 2nd edition (revised)/A Grand Tour of the Realms|74}}</ref><ref name="FRCS2Ep77"/><ref name="tCoRB-p147">{{Cite book/The City of Ravens Bluff|147}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/in-migrations}}
* Dwarven refugees of Roldilar retreat, going east, south over the seas, and to hidden, isolated communities still surviving in the Vast.<ref name="FRCS2Ep71"/><ref name="tCoRB-p144"/> Several clans flee into the [[Earthspur Mountains]].<ref name="tGHotRp94"/> Others, particularly craftsfolk and noncombatants migrate to [[Myth Drannor]] in [[Cormanthyr]].<ref name="LEoFp128"/><ref name="tGHotRp94"/>
* The dwarves leave the Vast to the humans, who stay to fight the orcs while more keep arriving. Thus the Vast passes entirely into human hands.<ref name="FRCS2Ep71"/><ref name="tCoRB-p144"/><ref name="tGHotRp94"/>


