{{Yearbox/in-politics}}
* The city of [[Thentia]] is founded by the [[Moonsea]].<ref name=tGHotR-p103>{{Cite book/The Grand History of the Realms|103}}</ref>
* In [[Shou Lung]], the last [[Emperor Chin]] of the [[Kao Dynasty]], along with his family, dies in a fire that razes the old [[Imperial City]]. [[Ton Bor]], the emperor's third cousin, is named the first [[Emperor Chin]] of the Yin Dynasty, meaning "Silver". Instead, Shou history records it as the [[La Dynasty]], meaning "Wax" for its malleability. Rival factions and secret societies influence the La emperors, and it is time of rampant corruption and poor management.<ref name=tGHotR-p103/>

{{Yearbox/in-migrations}}
* ''Circa'': [[Impiltur]]an settlers build their homesteads on the eastern side of the [[Easting Reach]]. From there, they expand south and inland around the [[Forest of Lethyr]] for the next fifty years.<ref name=tGHotR-p103/>

{{Yearbox/in-environment}}
* In [[Myth Nantar]], the shields around the [[Academy of the Dukars]], having slowly expanded since the city's collapse in [[720 DR]], now cause the city's ''[[mythal]]'' to become impenetrable to all matter and magic, permitting only water, [[coral]]s, [[fish]], and [[sea star]]s. When it is touched, the ''mythal'' appears to emit a haunting song. The legend arises that the city and the [[Dukars]] are cursed until they perform for all the races of [[Serôs]]. Over the five centuries, fewer and fewer people come to Myth Nantar.<ref name=tGHotR-p103/>

{{Yearbox/births}}
* [[Sammaster|Sammaster First-Speaker]], the future founder of the [[Cult of the Dragon]], is born. However, the whereabouts and exact date are lost to history.<ref name=tGHotR-p103/>


