* [[Nimoar|Nimoar the Reaver]] gathers an army and conquers [[Ulbaerag Bloodhand]]'s [[Bloodhand|tribe]]. They settle at [[Bloodhand Hold]] and renamed it [[Nimoar's Hold]], on the site that would later become [[Waterdeep]].<ref name="CoS.W-p8">{{Cite book/City of Splendors: Waterdeep|8}}</ref><ref name=GHR>{{Cite book/The Grand History of the Realms|108}}</ref>  
* In [[Ascalhorn]], [[demon]]s defeat the [[devil]]s and conquer the old elven citadel, which becomes known as [[Hellgate Keep]]. The [[elf|elven]] kingdoms of [[Eaerlann]] and [[Ammarindar (kingdom)|Ammarindar]] fall to the swarm of demons that emerges.<ref name=GHR/><ref>{{Cite book/Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting|270}}</ref><ref name="LEoF-p90">{{Cite book/Lost Empires of Faerûn|90}}</ref>
* The surviving monsters let loose by the [[Netherese]] of [[Ascalhorn]] overwhelm the [[dwarf]] realm of [[Ammarindar (kingdom)|Ammarindar]].<ref name=GHR/> 
* The city of [[Zhentil Keep]] launches a military campaign to deal with the growing problem of renegade [[liches]] roaming the city at night (also known as the period of the "[[Night Plague]]").<ref>{{Cite book/Ruins of Zhentil Keep/Campaign Book|28}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/in-politics}}
* The realm of [[Ardeep]] is resettled and rebuilt by [[moon elf]] refugees from [[Eaerlann]]. They ally with the [[dwarves]] of the [[Forlorn Hills]] and [[human]]s living along the [[Delimbiyr]], in an alliance called the [[Fallen Kingdom]] (the same name as [[Phalorm]]), but this quickly collapses owing to suspicions about human involvement in the fall of Ascalhorn.<ref name=GHR/>
* In [[Citadel Sundbarr]], the dwarves allow the human refugees of the demons to settle in their surface strongholds.<ref name=GHR/>
* The king of [[Maurmurra]] in the [[Vilhon Reach]] is slain by [[Kalgrathur Daycloaks]], leader of the [[Nightfire Lances]] mercenary army. Kalgrathur names himself High Lord of Maurmurra.<ref name=GHR/>  

{{Yearbox/deaths}}
* Prince [[Simberuel Astalmé]] of [[Ascalhorn]] was killed by [[vrock]]s while protecting the [[dwarf|dwarven]] [[Forgemaster of Sundbarr]] in the [[Turnstone Pass]].<ref name="SM-p66">{{Cite book/Silver Marches|66}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/misc}}
* [[Ghaurin]], scion of the adventurous dwarven [[Stoneheart]] clan tries to defend his ancestral home from the fiends out of Ascalhorn. After praying to [[Moradin]] to save the mansion, an earthquake seals off the underground portion and Ghaurin himself is transformed into a sentient [[stone golem]].<ref name="LEoF-p89">{{Cite book/Lost Empires of Faerûn|89}}</ref>
* The [[bard]] [[Maerstar]], one of the few humans to have escaped the massacre that occurred at Ascarlhorn, composes a song that rechristens the fortress as [[Hellgate Keep]].<ref name="HG-p5, 8">{{Cite book/Hellgate Keep|5, 8}}</ref>


