{{Yearbox/in-conflicts}}
* The [[Battle of Many Arrows]]: [[Citadel Felbarr]] is captured by an [[orc]] horde led by [[Obould (original)|Obould]]. Afterward, Felbarr is known as the Citadel of Many Arrows.<ref name="LEoF-p85">{{Cite book/Lost Empires of Faerûn|85}}</ref><ref name="TGHotR-119">{{Cite book/The Grand History of the Realms|119}}</ref>
* A legion of orcs assaults [[Tethyamar]]. They are bolstered by [[barghest]]s, and [[demon]]s summoned through [[circle magic]] wielded by an [[archmage]] alleged to be [[Great Hlundadim]] and a number of orcish [[adept]]s.<ref name="TGHotR-119"/>

{{Yearbox/migrations}}
* The [[dwarf|dwarven]] refugees of the [[Iron House]] of Tethyamar flee to the [[Storm Horns]] and [[Far Hills]].<ref name="TGHotR-119"/>

{{Yearbox/births}}
* [[Szass Tam]] is born. He will later become the the [[Zulkir]] of [[Necromancy]] in [[Thay]].<ref name="S.CG-110">{{Cite book/Spellbound/Campaign Guide|110}}</ref><ref name="TGHotR-119"/>

{{Yearbox/in-people}}
* Lord [[Vanrak Moonstar]], a famed explorer, goes on a failed expedition to the [[Black Jungles]] of [[Chult]].<ref name="TGHotR-119"/> He returns to [[Waterdeep]] a pale shadow of his former self. After his father dies, he assumes leadership of House [[Moonstar (family)|Moonstar]] and publicly splits with the [[High House of Stars]], blaming them for his father's death and secretly embracing [[Shar]].<ref name="CoSW-45">{{Cite book/City of Splendors: Waterdeep|45}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/deaths}}
* Lord [[Andvarran Moonstar]] dies of a mysterious wasting disease unknown to [[Waterdeep]]'s healers and strangely resistant to their spells.<ref name="CoSW-45" />


