* The [[Heralds of Faerûn]] split away from the [[Harpers]]/<ref name=GHR>{{Cite book/The Grand History of the Realms|119}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/in-conflicts}}
* A large pirate fleet is trapped by the navy of [[Dambrath]] off the coast of [[Timarl]] and defeated. Thirteen ships bearing pirate loot sink in waters over 200 feet (60 meters) deep.<ref name=GHR/>

{{Yearbox/in-politics}}
* In [[T'u Lung]], Emperor [[Shin Rokan]] attempts to take control of the armies away from the barons, raises taxes to fund them, and demands an oath of loyalty to the [[Lui]] Dynasty from everyone. For this, he is soon assassinated by [[Wai Long Hwa]], in turn naming himself emperor. The [[Ho]], [[Tan]], and [[Yang]] clans secede, marking the commencement of the "Three Kingdoms" period.<ref name=GHR/>
* From this point, [[Shou Lung]] makes fewer incursions into T'u Lung during its "Three Kingdoms" period, instead making separate diplomatic overtures to each kingdom in an effort to weaken and reabsorb them into the Shou empire.<ref name=GHR/>


